w (.github/workflows/test.yml) on the PR head to finish; if it fails, fix and push again until it is green.","verifier":"Verify the PR for https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/104 at its head commit, from the repository root. Run each check's commands; reading the diff alone is not enough. One check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1. Expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> [<file> ...] checks every file named in order and prints <file>:<line>: <error> for each bad row, as for one file before\"\nRun:\n```\nd=$(mktemp -d) && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > \"$d/c1.jsonl\" && printf '{\"c\":3}\\n' > \"$d/c2.jsonl\" && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{bad}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{oops\\n' > \"$d/b1.jsonl\" && printf '{x}\\n' > \"$d/b2.jsonl\" && node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/c1.jsonl\" \"$d/b1.jsonl\" \"$d/c2.jsonl\" \"$d/b2.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/b1.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/b2.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"d=$d\"\n```\nPASS: the four-file run prints exactly the lines of the b1 run (`<d>/b1.jsonl:2: ...` and `<d>/b1.jsonl:4: ...`) followed by the line of the b2 run (`<d>/b2.jsonl:1: ...`), in that order, with the same error text as the single-file runs and nothing for c1/c2. FAIL: any bad row missing, extra lines, wrong order, a different prefix or error text, or only the first file checked (before the change it prints nothing and exits 0).\n\nCheck 2. Expect: \"A file named - is read from stdin and reported as -; a second - is a usage error (exit 2)\"\nRun:\n```\nd=$(mktemp -d) && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n' > \"$d/c1.jsonl\" && printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{bad}\\n' | node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js -; echo \"exit=$?\"; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' | node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js -; echo \"exit=$?\"; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{bad}\\n' | node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/c1.jsonl\" -; echo \"exit=$?