ut. FAIL: any other exit code, the read error on stdout or absent from stderr, or the file after the missing one not reported.\n\nCheck 4. Expect: \"lint(text) in src/index.js is unchanged\"\nRun:\n```\ngit rev-parse HEAD:packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js\n```\nand\n```\nnode -e \"import('./packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js').then(({lint})=>{console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n\\n{bad}\\n{\\\"torn\\\":')))})\"\n```\nPASS: the blob hash is exactly 83cbf9f59ea8da3c9a2850def62de75a29dbb035 (the file before the change) and the second command prints `[{\"line\":3,\"error\":\"Expected property name or '}' in JSON at position 1 (line 1 column 2)\"},{\"line\":4,\"error\":\"Unexpected end of JSON input\"}]`. If the hash differs, FAIL only if the diff to packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js changes the lint function (its signature, body or behaviour); a hash differing because of changes outside lint is PASS only if lint's text is identical. FAIL otherwise.\n\nCheck 5. Expect: \"node:test tests cover two clean files, one bad among several, stdin via - (clean and bad), a missing file among good ones, two - arguments and no arguments; the package README documents the usage\"\nRun:\n```\nnpm test --workspace packages/jsonl-lint 2>&1 | grep -E '^(not )?ok|^# (pass|fail)'\n```\nand\n```\ngrep -n -e '<file> \\[<file> \\.\\.\\.\\]' -e '`-`' packages/jsonl-lint/README.md; echo \"grep=$?\"\n```\nThen read packages/jsonl-lint/test/*.test.js and packages/jsonl-lint/README.md.\nPASS: all tests pass (`# fail 0`), and the test files contain node:test tests that invoke the CLI for each of: two clean files, one bad file among several, stdin via - with clean input, stdin via - with bad input, a missing file among good ones, two - arguments, and no arguments; and the README documents the multi-file usage, - for stdin, and the exit codes. FAIL: any test failing, any of the seven cases not covered by a test, or the README not documenting the new usage.\n\nCheck 6. Expect: \"The change is o